SUMMARY: Found and cataloged three gate-passing layer-22 attention subsets. Preferred compact candidate [6,9,11]: GSM8K generation relative drops zero/mean 40.47%/42.86%, held-out 45.24%/45.24%, maximum control drop 3.19%. Strongest [6,9,10,11]: generation drops 47.61%/47.61%, held-out 59.53%/54.76%, maximum control drop 2.82%. Alternative [6,10,11]: generation drops 30.96%/33.33%, held-out 52.39%/50.00%, maximum control drop 2.93%. All passed both ablation methods and random-baseline gate (reported percentile 1.0). Selective MLP clusters in layers 21/22 grew from 256 to 512 neurons but yielded at most 4.76% generation damage. Proxy log-prob drops substantially understated attention-subset reasoning damage.
LESSONS: [
 "Layer-22 attention was the real signal: heads [6,9,10,11] cut GSM8K gen accuracy by 47.6% (zero and mean) and 54.8\u201359.5% on held-out, while max control drop stayed under 3.0%.",
 "Proxy NLL underestimated reasoning damage for attention: the same layer-22 4-head subset had only ~0.09 GSM8K score drop and small control effects, but generation accuracy fell by 0.476.",
 "Selective MLP clusters in layers 21/22 were much weaker: growing from 256 to 512 units only reached 0.0\u20134.8% GSM8K gen drop, far below attention heads.",
 "The compact 3-head subsets still validated well: [6,9,11] gave 42.9% gen drop on the main set and 45.2% on held-out, with max control drop 3.19%.",
 "Validation was useful: all three candidate head subsets passed, and each beat random subsets with random_gen_drops often near 0.0\u20130.29 and percentile 1.0."
]
